Package: katemark
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, kate
Description: Markdown preview beside the editor in Kate, with scroll sync
 Katemark shows the Markdown document you are editing in a panel beside the
 text, as GitHub would, and follows what you type and where you scroll. It
 draws tables, task lists, footnotes and syntax-highlighted code, math with
 KaTeX and diagrams with Mermaid, reads the CodiMD, Obsidian and MkDocs
 syntax, and exports to PDF and HTML.
 .
 The renderer, its styles and its fonts are inside the plugin, so the preview
 needs no network. A picture on the web is loaded only when the person turns
 that on in Katemark's page of Kate's settings; the same page has a button that
 asks GitHub for the latest release, used only when it is clicked. The plugin is
 off until it is ticked under Settings, Configure Kate, Plugins; the preview
 opens with Ctrl+Shift+M.
 .
 Katemark is Olivier Booklage's work, a fork of uwuclxdy's Katdown. This
 package is Sparky Stereo OS, Daniel Ramos's edition of SparkyLinux (by Pawel
 "pavroo" Pijanowski), built from the release's source with the edition's own
 Qt and KDE libraries.
